id: pm-todos-checklist-hierarchy
title: Preview marked checklist hierarchy repairs before applying relations
description: "Acceptance: reindenting a marked child produces one native relation change; title similarity never chooses a parent; cycles and deleted parents refuse before writes; compact previews include affected ancestors and children only. Overlap rechecked: Markdown parsing and text/source sessions do not assign reviewed native hierarchy meaning. Reuse SDK graph topology validators, certified reads, verified native history and mutateItem; one field producer drives preview and locked writes. Native staged-copy preview limitations are tracked in pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview. Selected targets are revalidated inside the native item lock; sibling targets retain a documented last-read window. No package journal or frozen recovery plan."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: "gh:unbraind/pm-todos#168",hierarchy,markdown,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T00:32:09.934Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T03:30:34.199Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:32:34.510Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against current core public declarations and sibling graph, CSV and beads docs: no marked checklist repair contract exists. Reuse previewItemMutations for native validation and update for persistence, RelationshipGraph for affected topology, verified history for revision guards. Core transactions serialize transactions only (upstream #1620); re-read every guarded target immediately before writes and document the remaining ordinary-writer window. No SDK pin change, no git requirement."
  "2026-10-29T00:41:16.972Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the shared relation planner, strict revision sidecar schema, native staged validation/update path, bounded receipts and hierarchy CLI. Targeted non-git tests already verify single-child reparenting, exact-ID selection, orphan/jump refusals and ordinary-writer ABA boundaries. Apply is deliberately per-item with truthful partial-progress receipts; it has no frozen mutable journal or package-owned lease, and the final SDK read-to-update window remains documented."
  "2026-10-29T00:53:46.451Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: in a disposable copy, reverting rows() to retain baseline targets made the one-child reindent regression fail (changed 0 instead of 1). Restoring the implementation passed the same regression; the package worktree was not mutated. Linked pm tests passed (typecheck and reindent regression). Real public-corpus reads exposed native previewItemMutations EACCES on immutable copied files; follow-up pm-todos-hierarchy-readonly-preview records the exact public signature and searches. No validator bypass or upstream write was made."
  "2026-10-29T00:55:39.035Z",codex-agent,"Read-only public validation measured 104 native items, 104 exported rows, zero skipped, 11189 Markdown bytes and 12293 sidecar bytes. Unchanged preview returned 104 unchanged. Two changed-preview attempts returned native EACCES, retained as a typed SDK limitation; every copied byte remained unchanged, with no git executable available. The corpus came from committed public main at d1202cf41d538ea11dc9a8967c6aabe64a9cf002. Source was only read through git archive."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:15.514Z",codex-agent,"Installed-path validation justified replacing unusable native staged-copy previews with shared core graph validation plus native mutateItem. Preview and the locked callback run one field producer. Every selected history revision is verified again inside the target item lock, and sibling-target races retain their documented last-read window. Host commands use the injected certified reader. The model now also covers moving an existing blocker between two parents, not only add/remove, so the old dependency is removed exactly once."
  "2026-10-29T01:08:54.442Z",codex-agent,"The final public read-only corpus validation now succeeds on both unchanged and changed previews: 104/104 rows exported, zero skipped, 104 unchanged; one relation proposal affects two rows in a 265-byte JSON receipt. No copied bytes changed and git was absent from PATH. Native staged-copy limitations remain a separate follow-up; the feature's shared native-field producer and SDK graph/mutation path avoid them."
  "2026-10-29T01:13:46.037Z",codex-agent,"The installed-artifact native-format state model passed all 500 seeded sequences: Markdown/tasklist projection, todo.txt, pi todo JSON, JSONL and checkbox; both importer names, sync, every exporter, producer validation, producer re-import, older input replay and CRLF variants. Full native documents were read back through the SDK and compared with an independent model, including preserved repaired parents, dependency annotations, body and every untouched native field. SDK date normalization supplies expected deadline values."
  "2026-10-29T01:23:11.579Z",codex-agent,"The final hierarchy model passed all 500 seeded sequences under random configured lifecycle registries and ambient focus. Targeted coverage measured hierarchy.ts at 99.70% lines / 90.98% branches / 100% functions and hierarchy-command.ts at 100% lines / 87.10% branches / 100% functions; full-package unchanged thresholds remain CI's gate. Packed npm-minimum acceptance passed on host 2026.10.23: two hierarchy rows, one applied relation, zero changes on replay; native source recovery and foreign copied-marker refusal also passed. A no-git CLI test fixture's missing declared peer link was corrected before final CI."
  "2026-10-29T01:26:58.528Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/pull/168. Final targeted no-git CLI, interrupted retry, multiple-blocker export and strict native ownership checks passed 4/4. The two 500-sequence models passed; npm-minimum packed acceptance passed. The released claim and append-only evidence are committed before the final CI push. Full npm and Bun release-gate receipts for the final head will be maintained in the PR; no merge or release is authorized."
  "2026-10-29T01:44:43.095Z",codex-agent,"The first exact-head CI run (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/actions/runs/40800575482, head 1c2903d) ran 447 tests: 446 passed and one new model assertion failed because the native writer added author_source, which the model's exact field set omitted. Coverage already met unchanged gates (99.25% lines, 93.58% branches, 99.71% functions on Node 26). The relation producer now explicitly declares author_source=asserted for its explicit author, and the model verifies it. The strengthened 500-format model with populated scope/source fields, sync-output replay and unchanged unselected parents passed locally. Final-head CI must rerun both npm and Bun gates after this correction."
  "2026-10-29T02:12:58.547Z",codex-agent,"CodeQL identified polynomial backtracking in the new rows() regex (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-todos/runs/123214465842). Replaced it with disjoint linear prefix/marker scans. A million-space malformed row now returns orphan_row within the bounded child-process test on Node 24 and Node 26. In a disposable copy, reverting only rows() made that child time out after 15 seconds; restoring rows() passed. Fresh exact-head CI and CodeQL scans are required for this correction; earlier release-gate successes are preliminary only. Topology checks now run only for changed relations, retaining complete selected-revision checks and avoiding repeated whole-graph validation for no-ops."
  "2026-10-29T02:53:29.243Z",codex-agent,"Re-review: fixing the general rule that every durable prefix of a multi-item repair must satisfy native topology, even when a later mutation refuses ownership or is interrupted. The branch is clean and includes origin/main. Auditing all package mutation and transport paths; preview and apply will share a safe persisted-transition schedule and locked revalidation. GitHub currently lists only the already-fixed CodeQL regex finding; no additional non-blocking findings are supplied in the review payload."
  "2026-10-29T02:59:39.208Z",codex-agent,"Class audit: hierarchy.ts is the only package path that edits existing native parent/blocker/dependency topology. Its SDK export and CLI JSON/TOON commands share applyTodoHierarchy. sessions.ts and source-sessions.ts have explicit field allowlists excluding relationships (including compensation); import/upsert/sync preserve existing relationships; recurrence creates a new successor and edits schedule/provenance fields only. Replaced final-graph-only assumptions with a native-validated sequence of single-item graphs, plus validation of the exact live intermediate graph inside each item lock. No temporary edge mutations, blind rollback, workspace-isolation claim, or threshold changes. Regression covers inverse blocks edges, strict foreign ownership, both interruption points, current-state retry and every SDK boundary; the existing 500-sequence model now randomizes entire forests and checks every persisted prefix. Packed npm/bun local/global acceptance now checks JSON/TOON refusal, unchanged native histories, release/re-export and safe completion."
  "2026-10-29T03:18:37.757Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: copied the package and new regression into a disposable non-git scratch copy, reverted ONLY applyTodoHierarchy to the reviewed HEAD implementation, and ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=persisted test/hierarchy.test.ts. It failed in validTopology with ordering_cycle_created for the three persisted fixture rows (expected no cycles). A finally block restored the fixed function; rerunning passed 1 test, 0 failures. The working implementation was never reverted. The 500 native import/export/sync model sequences have also passed across all five formats; the expanded hierarchy model is still running."
  "2026-10-29T03:23:56.684Z",codex-agent,"Validation update: the focused two-file run passed 16 tests (including all 500 native-format sequences) and canceled the hierarchy model at its unchanged 1,200,000 ms limit after more than 450 sequences on the saturated host. Existing assertions, 500 sequences and timeout remain unchanged. New topology checks now run after every persisted write instead of redundantly rereading unchanged graphs at all four boundaries; the dedicated adversarial test still checks every boundary. Rerunning that model alone. All 3 linked pm tests passed through pm test --run --progress (tracking remains disabled by existing policy). Exact disposable revert argv used --test-name-pattern=\"every persisted hierarchy prefix\"; the linked command uses the equivalent unique pattern persisted. The packed checker passed refusal/progress checks but its initial projected PmClient.get read omitted blocked_by; the checker now uses readLocatedItem for the full native document, as the state models already do."
  "2026-10-29T03:27:11.173Z",codex-agent,"Packed npm-current acceptance passed on pm 2026.10.25 using the shipped artifact: hierarchy export/preview/apply/replay, strict foreign prerequisite ownership with applied=0 and unchanged full native histories, release/re-export and safe two-write completion. The receipt reports hierarchy_prefix_safe=true. Other existing source ownership, compensation recovery and foreign-marker checks passed in the same consumer. JSON/TOON and all six local/global npm/Bun scenarios will run in each CI release gate."
  "2026-10-29T03:28:45.363Z",codex-agent,"Fresh read-only public-data validation on committed pm-todos main input d1202cf41d538ea11dc9a8967c6aabe64a9cf002: 104 items, 104 exported, 0 skipped; Markdown 11189 bytes, sidecar 12293 bytes; unchanged preview 104 unchanged; changed preview 1 relation, 2 affected rows, 265 JSON bytes; no staged refusals. The scratch copy was non-git, read-only and had no git executable on PATH; all copied bytes and the source stayed unchanged. Final local typecheck, build:test, docstring gate (25 files, 152 declarations) and diff whitespace checks passed. Native state checks use readLocatedItem rather than lossy list/get projections."
  "2026-10-29T03:30:30.547Z",codex-agent,"Final local validation: node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"500 seeded\" test/hierarchy.test.ts passed all 500 hierarchy sequences (1 test, 0 failures/cancellations, 387.7 seconds within the original timeout). Each actual persisted prefix is checked through native SDK reads; all original state/preservation assertions remain. Together with the earlier 16 passing focused tests, both 500-sequence models and all targeted scenarios are now complete. npm-current packed acceptance passed with hierarchy_prefix_safe=true; typecheck, build:test, docstring, changelog full/check, whitespace/privacy checks and all 3 linked pm tests passed. Re-review blocking class fixed across shared SDK/CLI/JSON/TOON paths; no other open non-blocking finding was supplied. Releasing only this agent claim. The final exact-head npm and Bun release gates (two workers, Node 22/26, six packed scenarios each) and run URLs/counts will be maintained on PR 168 after this final tracker commit; no merge or release."
